   00886| // Recognise a memory substitution (a read+write transform) in any language. A
   00887| // bare "replace X with Y" is an ordinary coding request, so a memory *scope*
   00888| // phrase must be present to claim the prompt. We then strip the scope and the
   00889| // substitution directive (position-independent: SVO languages lead, Hindi
   00890| // trails) and split the operand span on the connector to recover (old, new).
